## 2026-11-24 — Hard monkey test section (new capability)

- Answer to user question: WebDoctor had **no monkey/fuzz/chaos test mode** before this change. The only prior "monkey" references were pytest `monkeypatch` fixtures and a `SurveyMonkey (surveys)` tracker signature. This entry adds a real deterministic monkey suite.
- Files: `webdoctor/checks/monkey.py` (new), `webdoctor/config.py`, `webdoctor/runner.py`, `webdoctor/cli.py`, `webdoctor/reporters/markdown_report.py`, `webdoctor/reporters/html_report.py`, `webdoctor/server/app.py`, `webdoctor/server/templates/dashboard.html`, `webdoctor/server/static/dashboard.js`, `tests/test_monkey.py` (new), `README.md`, `last changes`.
- Change: added `run_monkey_check()` with a seeded random planner (default seed `20261124`, default `200` actions, max `500`), a full action trace and a deterministic config fingerprint. Actions include safe clicks, harmless typing, scrolling, keyboard navigation and viewport changes. Safety guards always block form submits (including `form.submit()`/`requestSubmit()`), POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE requests, downloads, destructive labels/URLs, password/file inputs, hidden/disabled controls, dangerous URL schemes and off-origin document navigation. Native dialogs are dismissed, never accepted; Enter is never pressed.
- Findings: `MONKEY_PAGE_CRASH`, `MONKEY_JS_E<signature>`, `MONKEY_CONSOLE_E<signature>`, `MONKEY_BLANK_PAGE`, `MONKEY_DIALOG`, `MONKEY_OFF_ORIGIN_BLOCKED`, `MONKEY_SUBMIT_BLOCKED`, `MONKEY_MUTATION_BLOCKED`, `MONKEY_RUNNER_ERROR`, plus navigation/options failures. Browser-suite JS/console errors are deduplicated by normalized signature before issue creation so identical faults do not receive double penalties, while different errors keep distinct hashed IDs.
- Integration: new keyword-only `monkey`, `monkey_seed`, `monkey_actions`, `monkey_delay_ms`, `monkey_navigation` parameters on `run_diagnostics()`. A skipped `Hard Monkey Test` suite is recorded when the site is unreachable or the browser suite is disabled. Monkey metrics are namespaced under `report.metrics["monkey"]` and `report.metrics["monkey_actions_executed"]` so browser metrics are never overwritten. `--monkey` is rejected with `--no-browser`. Both `check` and `demo` CLI parsers support the new flags; the dashboard exposes a checkbox, seed/actions/delay/navigation controls, a summary badge/stat and validated request fields. `/api/progress` still returns only the existing secret-free whitelist.
- Reports: Markdown and HTML render a dedicated **Hard Monkey Test** section with seed, status, action counts, safety-block counters, run fingerprint and a per-step trace table. JSON carries all monkey data through `CheckResult.metrics`; PDF inherits the HTML section through WeasyPrint.
- Reason: the user asked whether WebDoctor performs monkey testing and requested a hard/best monkey-test section if absent. The implementation is accuracy-first: reproducible seeds, bounded actions, no destructive side effects, no double-counted findings, and honest skipped/failed states.
